# ── PoesIA environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` and fill in the providers you use:
#     cp .env.example .env
# `poesia` loads `.env` from the current directory automatically at startup
# (best-effort). Variables already exported in your shell take precedence.
# Never commit the real `.env` — it is gitignored.

# ── GalerIA: Cloudflare Workers AI (free tier, reliable) ────────────────────
# Needs a free Cloudflare account. Get both values from the dashboard:
#   Workers AI -> "Use REST API" -> Create a Workers AI API Token
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=your-account-id
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=your-workers-ai-api-token
#
# Usage: poesia galeria illustrate poem.txt --backend cloudflare
# Note (live-verified 2026-08-03): output is novel per request — the served
# SDXL wrapper does NOT honour the seed parameter. Use `--backend procedural`
# or `--backend pollinations` when reproducibility matters.

# ── GalerIA: Pollinations.ai (free, NO key required) ─────────────────────────
# Works out of the box with zero configuration:
#   poesia galeria illustrate poem.txt --backend pollinations
# Anonymous limit ≈1 image / 15 s; register at auth.pollinations.ai to raise it.

# ── GalerIA: hosted providers (paid / trial credits) ─────────────────────────
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=r8_...
# Usage: poesia galeria illustrate poem.txt --backend openai|replicate

# ── LLM generation (poesia write) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# The same host variables drive the LLM backends (groq / gemini / openai):
#   GROQ_API_KEY=...          GEMINI_API_KEY=...          OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# Ollama is local: OLLAMA_HOST=http://localhost:11434  OLLAMA_MODEL=gemma2:2b

# ── MLflow (training pipeline) ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# See .env_mlflow.example for the PostgreSQL-backed MLflow configuration.
